From: Sleepy <sleepy@localhost>
Subject: Revert "drm/amd/display: Consult MCCS FreeSync cap only if requested & supported"
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:30:00 +0000

This reverts commit cfdcf5571c3107bf636002fc0c16ce93c19bd671
("drm/amd/display: Consult MCCS FreeSync cap only if requested &
supported"), adapted to the 1163 form already in the series.

Upstream moved the MCCS clear inside the do_mccs gate. The later
do_mccs=false pass from amdgpu_dm_connector_ddc_get_modes() then
re-advertises VRR (freesync_capable = true -> vrr_capable = 1) on
HDMI sinks whose MCCS VCP does not answer. The MSI MAG251RX
(AMD VSDB v1, 48-240 Hz, MCCS flag, no HF-VSDB VRR) is such a sink:
on rc3 it shows vrr_capable=1 / passive_vrr_capable=1 while CachyOS
7.3 (rc2-based, which still has the unconditional clear) shows 0 for
the same EDID. Restore the unconditional clear, keeping the HF-VSDB
VRR exemption from 1163, so the advertisement matches the cachy
kernel that was verified clean on this monitor.

Signed-off-by: Sleepy <sleepy@localhost>
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -3948,17 +3948,26 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
-	if (do_mccs) {
-		dm_helpers_read_mccs_caps(adev->dm.dc->ctx, amdgpu_dm_connector->dc_link, sink);
-
-		/*
-		 * HF-VSDB VRR sinks keep freesync_capable even when the MCCS
-		 * read does not answer: the panel negotiates VRR through the
-		 * HDMI Forum VSDB, not the AMD MCCS VCP. Clearing the flag here
-		 * stops FreeSync signalling and leaves such panels (G-Sync
-		 * Compatible included) in a half-negotiated state that flickers.
-		 */
-		if (sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code && !sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported &&
-		    !connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.supported)
-			freesync_capable = false;
-
-		if (sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported && freesync_capable)
-			dm_helpers_mccs_vcp_set(adev->dm.dc->ctx, amdgpu_dm_connector->dc_link, sink);
-	}
+	if (do_mccs)
+		dm_helpers_read_mccs_caps(adev->dm.dc->ctx, amdgpu_dm_connector->dc_link, sink);
+
+	/*
+	 * HF-VSDB VRR sinks keep freesync_capable even when the MCCS
+	 * read does not answer: the panel negotiates VRR through the
+	 * HDMI Forum VSDB, not the AMD MCCS VCP. Clearing the flag here
+	 * stops FreeSync signalling and leaves such panels (G-Sync
+	 * Compatible included) in a half-negotiated state that flickers.
+	 *
+	 * The clear stays outside the do_mccs gate on purpose. Upstream
+	 * cfdcf5571c31 moved it inside; the later do_mccs=false pass from
+	 * amdgpu_dm_connector_ddc_get_modes() then re-advertises VRR on
+	 * HDMI sinks whose MCCS VCP does not answer (MSI MAG251RX).
+	 * CachyOS 7.3 (rc2-based) still carries the unconditional form and
+	 * reports vrr_capable=0 for these sinks; match that behaviour.
+	 */
+	if ((sink->sink_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A ||
+	     as_type == FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST) &&
+	    !connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.supported &&
+	    (!sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code ||
+	     (sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code && !sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported)))
+		freesync_capable = false;
+
+	if (do_mccs && sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported && freesync_capable)
+		dm_helpers_mccs_vcp_set(adev->dm.dc->ctx, amdgpu_dm_connector->dc_link, sink);

 update:
